{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/app selects its application host at open: it reads the binding from the log's opening records, selects one registered interpreter (workroom is the default), and folds with it. A binding names an application and fold version, must be signed by the initializing key, and has force only in the opening records. A repository bound to an application or fold this build does not hold stays kernel-verifiable and refuses to interpret or append. Init binds a new repository to the application it runs, recording that binding except for workroom, which absence names permanently, so every existing workroom log keeps its exact shape and the existing internal/app tests pass unchanged. kernel.ReadOpening is the bounded, authenticated, explicitly-not-a-verification read behind it. Gates at this head: go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test ./... -count=1, all 25 packages green.","body":{"commit":"135c4826168c04d7a520e8a644c9dab12d684884","path":"internal/app"}}